WEBVTT

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.690
Well, here we are again, ready to go.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.220
So today, I think I'll do a painting

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.020
that's a little bit different.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.260
Maybe we'll try to do a little covered bridge.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.220
I've been spending a lot of time in Indiana

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.200
the last few months,

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.710
and we've produced a series here in Indiana,

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.130
so let's do a little covered bridge.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.820
Indiana has a lot of covered bridges,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.180
so we'll start with a little bit of Alizarin Crimson

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.430
and Prussian Blue.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.900
Just mix them on the brush here,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.420
and let's just go right up in here and do like so.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.520
Just put in a little background color.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:09.810
I'm not worried about shapes or anything here.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:18.770
I'm just applying some background color, something like so.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.760
This is just a little Prussian blue and alizarin crimson.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.260
Now, the Prussian blue is many, many times stronger

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.060
than the alizarin crimson, so use very little of the blue.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.560
Okay, we'll wash the brush.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.040
I don't want to put some little trees

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.620
that are far back in the background.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.720
Okay, let's start with a one-inch brush,

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.220
and let's just go right into some cad yellow,

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.480
some yellow ochre, just mix them up here a little bit,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.980
a little tiny bit of permanent red.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.670
Maybe we'll have a little fall scene here

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.930
with a lot of colors in it.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.760
Okay, let's just go back in here

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.910
and just begin picking out some basic little shade.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.850
just barely touching and pulling down.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.390
I want to add a tiny bit of sap green to that.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.540
Still a little bit of green left back here.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.550
Oh yeah, that's much better.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.830
That stands out better.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.960
We'll just lay in some little basic shapes far, far back.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.860
We're not looking for detail, come later.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.990
Sort of vary your colors so they stand out a little bit.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.260
Don't kill all the little purplish color that you have here.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:34.700
Retain some of that.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.700
Let's let it work down.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.830
A little more green here.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:43.720
Sap green.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:44.700
There.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.620
Something like so.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.690
Distant, distant background.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.970
And just, as I say, bury the colors a little bit.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.690
Stand down there, nice yellow.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.410
Okay, now we'll take the large brush,

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.770
and very gently, I'm just gonna lift upward,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.790
just to soften this, make it look further away.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.600
There we go, that'll give us a quick little background.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.380
Now let's take the large brush

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.040
and we'll go right into some Sap Green,

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.330
a little bit of Alizarin Crimson,

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:43.390
and some Van Dyke Brown.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.120
Just mix them on the brush.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.350
Looking for a pretty dark color here.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.170
And we can begin dropping in some basic shapes.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.650
Really push that brush into the canvas, make it bend.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.580
There, all kinds of beautiful little shapes.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.940
Just let them fall off your brush.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.620
Alizarin, crimson, sap green,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.670
and a little bit of Van Dyke brown.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.050
Maybe there's a nice tree here

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:20.770
that just sort of hangs over all background.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.070
So we're really not worried about detail at this point.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.630
That gives us some nice basic background shapes.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.120
Little bit more right over in here.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:57.480
All righty.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.930
Now we can start playing with a little bit of detail.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.180
Take a little Van Dyke brown, tiny bit of umber in it,

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.650
but just put a happy little tree trunk right here.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:24.010
So arm out here, and most of this is gonna disappear.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.670
We're really not worried too much about it.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.240
Some of it will show through the leaves when we put them off.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.940
And we'll take a little bit of white

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.110
and add the same color to it.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.140
Just a little highlight.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.120
This is just white with a little bit of brown,

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.240
a little bit of ombre in it.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.970
Just puts a little indications here and there.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.700
Maybe there's a few more little things that live back here.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.330
Just indications.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:58.450
Maybe over here, nice little tree trunk too.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:05:59.900
Don't want it to be left out.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:07.730
Okay, now we can go in here,

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.360
take a little bit of cad yellow, sap green,

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.110
and we can begin laying some highlights on these.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.490
Touch, push the brush upward, make it bend a little bit.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.720
Brush needs to bend.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:34.910
I don't want it to get too bright yet.

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.090
We'll brighten it up in the foreground.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:55.400
Down in here, a little bit of yellow ochre,

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.320
just so that one stands out.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:01.970
Here I'm using the brush sideways

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.350
and making it bend upward,

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.370
just to create all these nice little grassy things.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.100
And we do them in layers,

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.860
starting in the back and working forward.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:14.150
Okay, let's move over to the other side of the canvas here.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:21.980
Make some leaves on some of these little trees and bushes.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:38.180
Right there, using the brush sideways again

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.820
to create little grassy areas.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:52.790
Let's go up here to this old big tree, leaves on him.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.750
Just drop them in, it's your creation.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.250
Tiny bit of paint thinner to my brush there,

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.330
just to thin the paint down so it'll stick easier.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.680
Ooh, a lot of nice foliage here.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.620
Be some good practice.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.940
Go right in here and drop in a few more

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.820
little bushes and stuff that stand out.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:43.150
Okay, now, maybe back here in the background,

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.260
maybe there's a little road.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.810
Maybe it just goes right around the corner back here.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.100
It just comes right out like this.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.000
Straight Van Dyke brown to start with.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.560
Dark on so the light will show.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:08.660
Take some brown and white.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.740
I'm gonna put a touch of blue into it.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.200
Just a touch, just a touch.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.280
Highlight on here, goes through the woods.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.120
A little tiny bit more of the yellow and green.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.770
I wanna set that road down into the painting.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.680
Some of the bushes come up over the road.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.780
That helps create the illusion of distance

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.230
like it's going back around the corner.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:40.640
We don't know where it's going, don't care, just let it go.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:50.580
Go back into some good dark color here,

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.730
Sap Green, Van Dyke Brown.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.460
Maybe this time we'll even add a little bit

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:57.780
of Prussian Blue to it to really darken it up.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:03.850
right in here, throw some very, very dark color.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.620
Mostly green though, very dark.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:20.630
And this side, Van Dyke brown, sap green,

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.820
tiny little bit of Prussian blue,

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.020
just to be very, very dark.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:35.040
Okay, I think it's time we started playing a little bit with the bridge.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:36.300
This is where the fun starts.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:43.170
And probably one of the easiest ways for you to learn how to do these fantastic little buildings and bridges and stuff.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:47.610
Let's go in here and very gently, let's just scrape out a basic shape.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:52.230
And maybe we're looking at a covered bridge and we're looking right through it so we can see the road behind it.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:58.900
So let's go right up in here and just take and lay in a very basic shape.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.940
So this is gonna drive you up the wall

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.000
when you start scraping out all your beautiful painting.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:07.670
And I don't wanna kill all this.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.370
I wanna be able to see it through the bridge.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:16.140
Just take that and try to save quite a bit of it here.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.000
You'll be able to see through it.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:22.520
Just scrape out your basic shape.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.580
So this gets rid of some of the loose thin paint.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.940
makes the next layer of paint stick much easier.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.580
This will help you, it's also a nice way

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.320
to sort of lay out your perspective a little.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.390
Okay, we'll go right into some Van Dyke Brown,

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.940
and let's go right up here

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.920
and begin building our little covered bridge.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.520
Just recently I found out, while I was here in Indiana,

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:57.640
why they built covered bridges.

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.960
Always thought it was a place you could...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.550
to go and get out of the rain or something.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.370
And the reason they covered these bridges

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.630
was to protect the structure

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.010
so the weather wouldn't get to it.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.980
It really wasn't the reason I thought it was at all.

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:13.850
So I learned something.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.200
Okay, here I'm gonna just lift upward with a little brown.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:19.140
All I'm gonna do is fill all this in with the brown,

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.140
and then we can begin working on detail.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.830
Fill in the entire thing with nothing but Van Dyke brown.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:35.020
Make us a nice edge, just right down like that.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:38.210
That edge up.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.880
This old bridge, he's had a hard life.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.620
He's not in the best of repair.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:59.920
Side over here, here, fill all this.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.120
That's the beauty of using a big knife.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.100
You can just drop things right in, no problem.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.970
Okay, now we have to do this bridge in stages,

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.940
and we do the part that's farthest away first, come forward.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:21.520
So I want to be able to see through this bridge,

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:26.170
so we'll do the back of it first, and then come forward.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.280
Down here, we can just fill all that in.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.430
Just fill it in, a lot of brown.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:50.620
You're sitting at home saying,

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.300
boy, he's messed up this time.

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:57.580
You may be right, but let's just see what happens here.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.740
In the background, we want very, very little light back here.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.760
Not a great deal's gonna show back here,

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.950
just some little indications, don't overdo.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.320
Just some very faint indications,

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.980
so when we put the front of the bridge on, it'll show better.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:20.090
Little tiny highlight here,

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.490
this is just a little brown and white,

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:26.870
just a little light playing right across there.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.380
Just a little.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:36.330
Now we can start working on the front of the bridge.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:42.120
And take some brown, Van Dyke brown, some umber, white.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:44.800
Just look like old wood.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.200
Don't over mix your paint.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.840
Leave it sort of marble-y here.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.660
So that way all these colors will happen

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.600
right here in your bridge.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.930
Okay, now let's just take the small edge of the knife

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.020
and begin making some boards.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.980
Now maybe, maybe you can just scratch a line right here.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.560
through here if it'll help you a little bit

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.900
to give you an idea of where you want

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.000
the front of the bridge to be.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.910
That'll be our stopping point.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.250
So we take the small edge of the knife

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.330
and just start making some boards.

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.200
This one's made out of old slab boards,

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.220
just barely touching, pulling down.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:23.600
Leave some space in between them.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.590
See, these old bridges, some of them are in bad repair.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:29.790
They've really been beat to death.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:36.700
Just wanna make it look like old boards hangin' here,

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:56.230
way down here, just put you some boards in.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.560
The bridge has really had a rough life.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.970
He's come all the way down.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.150
Don't cover up all the dark, because back in here,

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:27.620
we want to give the impression that we can see in and over.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:35.380
little bit there, and those are very, very important here.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:38.760
Make it look like we can see through this bridge.

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.780
It's very dark, because it's all in shadow here.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:47.880
In shadow.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:00.870
There's wood things in here.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.380
Maybe there's a little beam right here

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:09.700
that we can see right across.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.710
This edge a little, a little more distance,

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.900
a little more depth in the bridge.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:28.830
Just straight Van Dyke Brown.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.320
Now, if you wanted to, you can take a little bit of brown

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.640
and create some boards here.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.780
I've just got a little tiny bit of brown on the knife,

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:42.980
just touching, just to create the illusion of wooden planks.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:50.830
Did you ever think that an old covered bridge

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:51.810
would be this easy to make?

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.110
Let it run down.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:01.420
I think so.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.730
Now then, I wanna leave this area right in here.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.680
Very, very dark to make it look like

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.080
there's a recessed area and water down there.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:12.410
Might even take and add a little bit of brown

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:13.510
right down here at the bottom.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:19.150
Really, really very dark, very, very dark.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:23.850
Fill the rest of the canvas up here

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:24.970
with a little bit of sap green.

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:45.340
And, and you can, now, come right along here,

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:49.570
put a little bit of highlight on the road, just a little.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.810
with a, let's take the little liner brush,

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:05.090
and we'll take a little paint thinner,

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.920
and mix a little bit of this brown

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.440
till it's just like water, very, very thin.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.040
Maybe there's some little cat tails that live right here.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:20.470
So we'll just put in some little stems, like so,

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.430
and then put a little cat tail in there,

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:26.960
and we just push real hard with a brush, bloop,

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.120
drop them in, see how easy that is?

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:32.370
just to give some little indications.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:33.770
Make it look like there's water here

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.550
without actually seeing any.

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.320
Just a few little indications.

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:50.000
Just one little fuzzy thing up on him.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:56.390
Okay, now, let's take the old fan brush

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:58.150
and I'm gonna add a little of the thinner

00:19:58.150 --> 00:19:59.970
to the fan brush to make this paint a little...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.470
a little bit thinner and load up some cad yellow,

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.940
yellow ochre, and we'll put some sap green into it.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:07.380
There we are.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.720
Now we can begin deciding where everything's at.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.470
Maybe there's some little grassy areas right here

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:20.280
that just come right down, just like so.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:27.480
The ridge isn't used too much anymore,

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:29.540
so the grass is beginning to take the road back.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.690
Nature has a way of reclaiming things.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.620
Here, you can do basically the same thing.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:42.720
Put in a few little highlights.

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:44.750
Leave this dark area.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.430
It'll make it look like water back in there,

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:48.590
like there's a recessed area where water could be.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.400
This is where you sort of clean up all the edges

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.120
and bring it together.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:08.370
Now no cover bridge painting would be complete

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.030
unless we had a big tree in it.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:12.490
So let's put a big old tree in it.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.340
Start with Van Dyke brown.

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:19.230
Tree lives here.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.970
Tree, a lot of brown.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:32.980
and just drop him right in.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.800
It's your world, so you put a tree where you want him.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:38.610
And when you're doing this at home,

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.090
don't worry about copying exactly what I'm doing here.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.650
These are only guides.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.300
They're only to give you ideas and to stir your imagination

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.960
and to show you how to make the equipment work.

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.300
These are only guides,

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.230
because everyone sees nature differently.

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:56.740
Put your dreams on canvas.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.640
Okay, let's give him a happy little limb right out here.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:12.080
Yes, maybe, maybe, who knows, there's a big limb.

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.070
There it is, just comes right out.

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:21.860
Sort of shadows the bridge, nice and cool in the summer.

00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:29.870
Recently I had the pleasure of doing some demonstrations at a...

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:31.720
Bridge Festival here in Indiana.

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:34.110
And I met some of the most super people,

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:37.140
fantastic people.

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.060
There's some limbs.

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:47.740
Now then, we can use a little brown and white,

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:50.030
and I'm gonna put a touch of permanent red in it

00:22:50.030 --> 00:22:51.910
just to brighten it up a tiny little bit.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:57.500
Right in here, and just put some highlights

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.230
right in this big tree.

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:06.130
Just let it go, so.

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:14.460
Now next week, if you're gonna paint along with us,

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:15.980
we'll be doing a white canvas.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:17.970
So, have your easel set up,

00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:20.840
and a little glass of tea right there beside you.

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.640
Ice tea freak, I was raised in the south,

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:27.860
and everybody there likes ice tea.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:32.180
a habit I never got over when I was in Alaska.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.380
While we got this brown going here,

00:23:38.580 --> 00:23:39.500
I'm gonna put a couple little,

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:42.310
maybe there's a little fence right here.

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:49.790
Post there, maybe there's another one right there.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.970
Little fence, you know.

00:23:53.170 --> 00:23:59.000
At times, maybe back in the horse and buggy day,

00:23:59.120 --> 00:23:59.980
maybe they'd had a little.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.640
too much to drink and they didn't go through here

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:04.120
too straight, so this was sort of to guide them through,

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:04.380
maybe.

00:24:11.530 --> 00:24:14.020
We'll put one more post out here with nothing on it.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.280
This one's already lost all of its boards.

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:24.140
Tiny little bit of highlight here

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:25.380
to make these posts look right.

00:24:32.910 --> 00:24:33.820
Yeah, nasty.

00:24:33.960 --> 00:24:37.330
Okay, now, let's go up here

00:24:37.330 --> 00:24:39.860
and put some leaves on this tree.

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:41.180
We'll just use the old big brush.

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:43.600
I'll just use some Sap Green and Van Dyke Brown.

00:24:46.020 --> 00:24:47.200
First we'll put the dark in,

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.520
just to give us some indications.

00:24:48.860 --> 00:24:53.040
Just some indications.

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:55.910
Then we'll come back and lay some highlights on all these.

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.500
There's a few lives right there.

00:25:04.316 --> 00:25:05.516
wherever you think they should be.

00:25:08.124 --> 00:25:09.464
I'll use a little bit of cad yellow.

00:25:09.888 --> 00:25:11.548
with the least little amount of sap green.

00:25:11.548 --> 00:25:13.728
And I want this bright enough so it stands out.

00:25:16.284 --> 00:25:18.284
Okay, some highlights right on here.

00:25:22.812 --> 00:25:23.812
off your brush.

00:25:25.660 --> 00:25:27.660
Just here and there.

00:25:30.410 --> 00:25:31.630
Sort of brings the painting together.

00:25:31.810 --> 00:25:34.390
The old covered bridge is down there

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:36.050
and the trees just hanging over it.

00:25:36.230 --> 00:25:40.400
Maybe you're doing this at home.

00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:41.780
Let your imagination go.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:43.280
Think of a million little scenes

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:44.900
that you could make out of this basic idea.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:49.550
Okay, now we can sort of clean up the bottom,

00:25:49.630 --> 00:25:52.330
and we're on the verge of having a finished painting here.

00:25:52.470 --> 00:25:54.780
Put a little grass around the bottom of this tree,

00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:58.860
just to cover up his little foots, big foots.

00:26:01.116 --> 00:26:03.116
so

00:26:05.404 --> 00:26:05.744
End.

00:26:06.204 --> 00:26:07.864
I think we're about ready to sign this one,

00:26:07.864 --> 00:26:09.544
so I'll take a little bit of the thin oil.

00:26:09.628 --> 00:26:10.588
A little permanent red.

00:26:18.684 --> 00:26:21.684
I'll just drop a happy little signature in here.

00:26:23.324 --> 00:26:24.984
And we hope you've enjoyed this painting

00:26:24.984 --> 00:26:26.324
half as much as we have.

00:26:26.844 --> 00:26:27.844
Really a pleasure.

00:26:28.188 --> 00:26:29.008
being here with you.

00:26:30.028 --> 00:26:32.528
and showing you some of these fantastic ideas.

00:26:33.772 --> 00:26:35.772
and we hope we bring a little happiness into your life

00:26:35.772 --> 00:26:37.112
and give you some ideas.

00:26:37.388 --> 00:26:38.228
and you too.

00:26:38.380 --> 00:26:40.820
We'll drag out your almighty brush and paint along with us.

00:26:41.388 --> 00:26:42.888
So from all of us here.

00:26:43.212 --> 00:26:43.992
We'd like to wish you.

00:26:44.172 --> 00:26:45.172
Happy painting.

00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:46.100
God bless.

00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:47.140
See you next week.
